    773	### C11 — D17.b: Discrete Morse on the squarefree-only divisibility Hasse diagram (NEW from S232 follow-up)
    774	**Edges/sources:** D17 closed at S232 (mode E, B-grade) with sharp
    775	identity `collapses(N) = (π(N) − π(N/2)) + Π_pow(N) + 1` for the full
    776	divisibility Hasse 1-skeleton. The squarefree-only restriction is a
    777	distinct combinatorial object: vertices are `{n ≤ N : μ(n) ≠ 0}`,
    778	covering relations are still `n | m` with `m/n` prime.
    779	**Question:** Build `H_N^{sqfree}`, run the same greedy random Morse
    780	collapse, and measure `m_0(H_N^{sqfree})`, `m_1(H_N^{sqfree})`. Does
    781	the squarefree restriction inherit the boolean lattice's known
    782	shellability such that `m_0 = polylog N`, or does it match the same
    783	linear scaling as the full lattice?
    784	**Why this is a real successor (not a duplicate of D17 closure):** the
    785	divisibility lattice on `{n ≤ N : μ(n) ≠ 0}` is *isomorphic* (as a
    786	poset) to the truncation of the boolean lattice on primes ≤ N to
    787	"subsets `S` with product `≤ N`." The boolean lattice itself has order-
    788	complex of single critical cell at the top — radically smaller `m_0`.
    789	The truncation might preserve much of this collapsibility.
    790	**A-grade target:** `m_0(H_N^{sqfree}) = O(polylog N)` would give a
    791	*polylog combinatorial encoding of `μ²(n)` (squarefree primality
    792	witness)* — first known polylog topological compression of any
    793	arithmetic indicator. Even if not directly applicable to `χ_P`, this
    794	would be a *partial-positive Correlation-Dichotomy-shaped result* on
    795	the adjacent problem of squarefree counting.
    796	**B-grade outcome:** `m_0(H_N^{sqfree})` exhibits an analogous
    797	arithmetic identity (e.g., `~ Σ_{ω(n) > c} 1`) — a refined negative-
    798	shape result orthogonal to D17.
